/// Checks mobs, `world.mob` (CAL-156): a mooshroom as it's made, its turn drawn after its UUID and
/// its health its most; finalized as natural spawning finalizes it from the level's random, its
/// follow range's random spawn bonus and its hand, a pack's first never a baby and the rest one at
/// its chance, a baby half the size; whether it goes, `checkDespawn`; its saved tag, read back the
/// same; and one in a level's entities on stone, ticked in their tick list, mooing now and then
/// as its own random says. Then the other farm animals: each one's size and sounds, a chicken's
/// egg time drawn after its turn; their variants picked by the biome's selectors and drawn with
/// their sound variants as `finalizeSpawn` draws them; a sheep's color by its climate, pink 1 in
/// 500; their tags read back the same; and a chicken falling slowly and laying its egg. And
/// horses and donkeys: their sizes, `finalizeSpawn`'s draws, a horses' pack sharing its variant;
/// their health brought within its most on their first tick, healing and grazing; and their tags
/// read back the same. And equipment: what a mob's given found on its next tick and shown, then
/// nothing, its hands swapped shown as an event, and its slots saved and read back. And monsters:
/// local difficulty; each one's kind, size and sounds, the hostile source's; a zombie's, skeleton's
/// and spider's `finalizeSpawn` drawn as vanilla draws it, with a baby zombie's new chicken and a
/// spider's skeleton made and finalized, armor by its tier on hard, a skeleton's bow and a
/// Halloween pumpkin; a monster's tick in light; a creeper swelling; and their tags read back. And
/// the slime: made of size 1, finalized to its size by `Mob`'s draws then its own, landing with
/// its particles' draws and its squish, and its tag read back. And the zombie villager, its
/// profession drawn as it's made and its type by the biome as it's finalized; the witch, its
/// finalizing's draws and each tick's for its potions and particles; and the enderman; with their
/// tags read back. And the zombie horse, its rider made and finalized before its own draws. And
/// pushing: mobs side by side pushing each other as they tick, not one where its chunk doesn't
/// tick, a player pushing and pushed, and the cramming's draw. And mobs hurt in their own tick
/// (D424): a cow drowning till it dies, its loot table's left to its level, and one below the
/// level; one in a wall (D425); and one falling onto stone, hurt by its fall as it lands, its hurt
/// sound after the fall's sounds (D477). And spears (D480): the iron spear's components read as
/// their codecs read them, its conditions, a zombie's use of it, and what it hit spared a while.
module test.mob

import nbt.snbt.{parse}
import nbt.tag.{Tag}
import random.legacy.{LegacyRandom}
import world.damage.{Damage}
import registry.builtin.{builtin_entries}
import registry.registry.{Registry, Tag as RegistryTag}
import resources.identifier.{Identifier}
import server.log.{Entry}
import world.attributes.{Wearing, attribute_id}
import world.body.{BodyFacts, EntitySound, HOSTILE_SOURCE}
import world.difficulty.{LocalDifficulty, moon_brightness}
import world.chunk.{BlockStates}
import world.collision.{Aabb, CollisionBlocks}
import world.entities.{EntityTicking, Entities, StackSizes}
import world.entity_data.{AIR_SUPPLY, BABY, HEALTH, MOB_FLAGS, MOOSHROOM_TYPE, NO_AI_FLAG, Value}
import world.entity_facts.{CREATURE, MONSTER}
import world.experience_orb.{Follower}
import world.inside.{Rain}
import world.living.{Hurt, LivingFacts, Shown, Warding, kinetic_of, reach_of, view_vector}
import world.loot.{LootParams}
import world.modes.{Difficulty}
import world.goals.{Goal, GoalSelector}
import world.mob.{BABY_START_AGE, CHICKEN, COW, CREEPER, DONKEY, ENDERMAN, HORSE, MONSTER_OWN, Making, Mob, MobLight, OWN, Occasion, PIG, SHEEP, SKELETON, SLIME, SPIDER, SpawnGroup, Unmade, WITCH, VILLAGER, ZOMBIE, ZOMBIE_HORSE, ZOMBIE_VILLAGER, type_name}
import world.movement.{MovementStates}
import world.navigation.{NavLevel, SentBlock}
import world.paths.{PathTypeCache}
